-- so the count is two in the middle and one at either end, which is the shape of a pH-rate profile read
-- through an observation: the same molecule, the same instrument, the same temperature, and the number of
-- signals rising and falling with the acidity of the solution. A record with a field for the pH can hold
-- this; a record with a field for the structure cannot, and a record with a boolean for whether a catalyst
-- is present gets the middle case wrong in both directions.
ph-profile-has-a-minimum : (a : count-bath m-glucose-ph (bath-room 1 sol-acid) ≡ count-bath m-glucose-ph (bath-room 1 sol-water) → Empty) × (count-bath m-glucose-ph (bath-room 1 sol-base) ≡ count-bath m-glucose-ph (bath-room 1 sol-water) → Empty)
ph-profile-has-a-minimum = (λ q → transport (λ i → isTrue (eqb 1 ((concat (sym ph-acid) (concat q ph-neutral)) i))) unit , λ q → transport (λ i → isTrue (eqb 1 ((concat (sym ph-base) (concat q ph-neutral)) i))) unit)
